## CREDIT DISCIPLINE — READ ONCE, APPLIES THROUGHOUT

There are two separate costs. Control both.

**Build-time cost** (this file, one-off) is controlled by the operator rules above: fresh session per phase, named-file context only, no `@workspace`, Edit mode.

**Runtime cost** (every developer request, forever) is controlled by what you build. These constraints are baked into the Phase 3 and Phase 2 prompts and must not be relaxed:

- The orchestrator reads **exactly one** config file per request (`copilot-instructions.md`). It never enumerates `.github/skills/`, never opens a SKILL.md it has not routed to, never reads `playbooks/` to decide routing.
- Routing is **two-stage**: exact capability-token match first (zero model calls), LLM classification only on miss.
- `SKILL.md` is capped at **200 lines**. It is an index, not a manual. Detail lives in `playbooks/`, loaded only after the skill is selected.
- The orchestrator loads **one** playbook — the matched one. Never the folder.
- Installation is a **one-time** cost per workspace per agent. Already-installed agents skip clone entirely.
- Prerequisites (`requires:`) are declared **per skill**, not run globally. A request that does not need CodeGraph does not pay for it.

If a later change makes the orchestrator read more than one file before routing, you have lost the cost control and should revert it.

