## PHASE 8 — Acceptance run

This is the only phase that uses **Agent mode**, and it is a test, not a build. Start a fresh chat, attach nothing, and run these five prompts one at a time. Record each result.

| # | Prompt | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `/nexus-install` | Table of all active agents with install state. No installs performed. |
| 2 | `/nexus-install-<one active agent>` | `COMPLETED`, skill folder created. |
| 3 | Repeat prompt 2 | `ALREADY_INSTALLED`, no clone, near-instant. |
| 4 | One of your real Example Phrasings, in plain language | Routes to the correct agent, executes, returns one status. |
| 5 | A deliberately vague request, e.g. "make this repo better" | `NEEDS_CLARIFICATION` with three candidate capabilities. **Not** a guess. |

Then run `validate-registry.ps1` — expect exit 0.

**If test 5 returns anything other than NEEDS_CLARIFICATION, stop and revisit Phase 3 STEP 1.** Silent misrouting is the failure mode that erodes trust in the whole system, and it is the hardest to detect once developers are relying on it.

